WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.920
This lacy stitch pattern is an easy one

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:08.900
to work and remember,
with no cheat sheet needed.

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.300
Cast on a multiple of five
stitches plus two.

4
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.860
For my scarf, I cast on 25
stitches plus two for the edge.

5
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.020
To keep the edges neat.

6
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.340
There are two needles and work on each
side with no transfers over these needles.

7
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:29.180
I started by knitting two rows and ended
with the carriage on the right.

8
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:34.160
That's not critical,
but be consistent for your entire scarf.

9
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:44.480
The stitch pattern consists of
transferring stitches to a center needle.

10
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.500
First, transfer to the right,

11
00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:56.300
knit two rows, and then transfer
to the left and knit two rows.

12
00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:59.040
Alternating the transfers
creates the lace.

13
00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.200
To

14
00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:23.180
make things easier, I marked
my needle bed with a dry erase pen.

15
00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:25.490
You can also use a pencil.

16
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.400
This made it a no-brainer as

17
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.880
to which needles were
the center needles each time.

18
00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.240


19
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.480
after you work your transfers,

20
00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:40.700
make sure the empty needles are in working
position before you knit the next row.

21
00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:44.140
Do this on every transfer row.

22
00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.020
Now don't get lost if you
need to take a break.

23
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.620
Either keep track of your row counter,

24
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:55.140
for example, transfer right on row two,
transfer left on row four,

25
00:01:55.170 --> 00:02:02.180
right on row six,
left on row eight, or read your knitting.

26
00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:04.850
This is my center stitch.

27
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.660
Looking below, I can see the large
eyelet from the previous transfer.

28
00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.220
This tells me that I'm
transferring right on this row.

29
00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.500
That's it.

30
00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:20.080
A pretty and easy stitch
pattern with beautiful results.

31
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.400
When you've knit your required number

32
00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:29.060
of rows or you're running out of yarn,
knit two rows plain and bind off loosely.

33
00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:32.520
Block your scarf and enjoy.
Happy knitting.

